    {
        "_comment": "Run 1A COL5 (COL5Poly) muon stops for Michael MacKenzie's request. The Run 1A beam pools (MuBeamCat.MDC2025ab) are scored at the DS entrance, past COL5, so this resamples the Run 1B pool MuBeamCat.Run1Bai, scored at TS3 and built on geom_run1_a with the Hayman target, through geom_run1_a and the default Run 1A field. Only polyStopPath runs, with no prescale (Run 1B rode on the flash job at 1/1000). Smoke 2026-11-03 at MDC2025bb, 10,000 draws: 341 stops (335 mu-, 6 mu+), 17.8 ms per draw, VmHWM 2.14 GB, 2.2 kB per stop. 100 x 100,000 draws = 10M draws, under the 25.6M-event pool, for about 335k mu- stops (Run 1B MuminusPolyStopsCat.Run1Bap has 304k); about 30 min and 7.5 MB per job. MuBeamCat.Run1Bai has no resilient copy (only MDC2025ab and Run1Baa do), so inloc is tape; all 200 files were ONLINE on 2026-11-03. The first push (inloc resilient) registered cnf .0.tar and then failed the input check, so the campaign is .1.tar via --extend.",
        "desc": "PolyStops",
